/-!
# Associative free-algebra attachments and their word-stage endpoint

For an actual monoid `A`, an arrow `f : K ⟶ L`, and a monoid map from
`tensorWordMon K` to `A`, the word cubes in `MonoidWordPushoutFiltration`
construct a countable diagram with degree-zero object exactly `A.X`.
This module constructs multiplication on that diagram and its colimit.
Concatenation multiplies the two adjacent old coefficients, while all other
old coefficients and new letters retain their order.

`stageMul` descends through both actual finite-stage coequalizers.
`endpointMul` descends through the tensor product of the two actual countable
colimits. The left-unit, right-unit, and associativity diagrams are proved
from their values on every word pair or triple. Thus `endpointMonoid` has its
constructed unit, multiplication, and laws.

`endpointEvaluationMap` maps to every compatible original monoid target and
preserves both original old and free new-algebra maps. The endpoint comparison
identifies this actual monoid with the pushout of the original free-algebra
diagram. The literal word boundary is identified with the iterated pushout
product of `f` tensored with all `n + 1` old coefficient factors, including
degrees zero and one.

Only cocompleteness, closedness, and symmetry enter the construction. These
give the separate tensor colimit preservation required for the word-stage
arguments; the object, morphism, and colimit universes are independent.

`originalWordCellComplex` retains this same diagram as a native relative-cell
history, and `originalWordPushout_mem_cellularClosure` puts its original old
map in the existing cellular-closure API. The final associative-carrier bridge
retains the original associative free generator, adjunction unit, and entire
original free-algebra diagram through its canonical tensor-word comparison.
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

universe u v w

namespace CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory.MonoidWordPushout

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory TensorWord
open scoped MonoidalCategory MonObj

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [MonoidalCategory C] [SymmetricCategory C]
variable [MonoidalClosed C] [HasColimitsOfSize.{w, w} C]

